  "content": {
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "order": 1,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s1",
            "text": "Most of the ocean is a mystery."
          },
          {
            "id": "s2",
            "text": "We have to use powerful cameras to see what it’s like."
          },
          {
            "id": "s3",
            "text": "We’ve found mountains, canyons, and even waterfalls under the sea."
          },
          {
            "id": "s4",
            "text": "But cameras cannot show us everything."
          },
          {
            "id": "s5",
            "text": "We have to see for ourselves."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "order": 2,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s6",
            "text": "Jacques Piccard was a scientist who studied the oceans."
          },
          {
            "id": "s7",
            "text": "He wanted to reach the deepest part of the ocean."
          },
          {
            "id": "s8",
            "text": "So, he built a submarine."
          },
          {
            "id": "s9",
            "text": "He called the place he found “Challenger Deep” because it was so hard to get to."
          },
          {
            "id": "s10",
            "text": "There, he found something amazing: fish and shrimp."
          },
          {
            "id": "s11",
            "text": "Nobody thought any creature could live that deep."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
